lease with a healthy production history. (I skipped v2.3.1-rc because it was only ever healthy in staging, not production.) Rollback status: `rolled_out` in all regions.\n3. **Opened incident INC-0001 (SEV2)** for checkout-api; the on-call engineer has been paged. The summary documents the failing v2.3.1 deploy, the rollback to v2.3.0, and recommended follow-ups (verify recovery, root-cause v2.3.1 before redeploying).\n\nSuggested next step: re-check `get_service_status` for checkout-api in a few minutes to confirm the error rate drops on v2.3.0.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by checking the current status and release history for checkout-api.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01UKyAUweeL3CHvLZaBYxNNp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01EmxkUt9mFFijU94eu5kJ22", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01FozywnuVJ6DeTnTSUEUwdc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Rollback is rolled out in all regions. Opening the SEV2 incident.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01WjXzKeKEJUw9bCSFwstKFR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the deploy of v2.3.1 (error rate 0.18 across us-east, us-west, eu-west). Per the platform runbook, the service was rolled back in all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production (v2.3.1-rc was only validated in staging and was not considered). Rollback status: rolled_out in us-east, us-west, eu-west. Follow-up needed: confirm health/error rate recovery on v2.3.0 and root-cause the v2.3.1 regression before any redeploy.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Done. Summary of actions:\n\n1. **Diagnosed**: checkout-api was running v2.3.1 in us-east, us-west, and eu-west, unhealthy with an 18% error rate.\n2. **Rolled back** checkout-api to **v2.3.0** in all three production regions \u2014 the most recent release with a healthy production history. (I skipped v2.3.1-rc because it was only ever healthy in staging, not production.) Rollback status: `rolled_out` in all regions.\n3. **Opened incident INC-0001 (SEV2)** for checkout-api; the on-call engineer has been paged. The summary documents the failing v2.3.1 deploy, the rollback to v2.3.0, and recommended follow-ups (verify recovery, root-cause v2.3.1 before redeploying).\n\nSuggested next step: re-check `get_service_status` for checkout-api in a few minutes to confirm the error rate drops on v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}]}]}